--- log ---
2026-05-03T00:00Z claude created — implementation ticket for 0012 design; all design questions resolved in 0012 log

--- body ---
## Context

0012 accepted. Replace the `Status:` header enum with a binary
closed/not-closed criterion. Decisions recorded in 0012's log:

- `Closed:` header is the canonical closure mechanism (in-place, no
  file move required).
- Path substring test (`closed` anywhere in path) is opt-in; projects
  that use directory-based organization get it for free.
- `pending` is dropped entirely.
- Migration is atomic: `erg migrate` converts all tickets in a repo,
  must run before the new binary is installed.

## Actions

### A. `rules/tickets.md` spec change

- Remove `Status:` from the headers table.
- Add `Closed:` header row: optional, non-repeatable, preamble only;
  value carries reason (PR reference, supersession note, "abandoned —
  out of scope", etc.).
- Document the closed/not-closed criterion:
  > A ticket is **closed** if at least one holds:
  > 1. The substring `closed` (case-insensitive) appears anywhere in
  >    the ticket's file path.
  > 2. The header `Closed:` appears in the ticket's preamble.
  > Otherwise the ticket is **not-closed** (open).
- Document that `Closed:` is forbidden in the log and body sections.
- Remove `pending` from all enum references.
- Update the example tickets in the spec accordingly.

### B. Validator (`tickets/tools/go/`)

- Remove `Status` from the known-headers set; reject it on sight.
- Add `Closed` as a known optional non-repeatable header, preamble-only.
- Enforce `Closed:` forbidden in log and body (the parser already
  section-tracks; add a check).
- Apply the closed/not-closed criterion: derive `Erg.Closed` from
  path OR preamble `Closed:` header (current `Status: closed` logic
  replaced).
- `erg ready` exclusion: use `Erg.Closed` (unchanged semantics,
  different source).

### C. `erg close` rewrite

Current behaviour: find `Status: open|doing` line, replace with
`Status: closed`.

New behaviour: append `Closed: <reason>` to the preamble (after last
existing header, before the blank line preceding `--- log ---`). Do
not touch any `Status:` line — the validator will reject the file if
one exists, so migration must have run first.

### D. `erg migrate` new subcommand

```
erg migrate [dir]
```

Idempotent. For every `.erg` file under `dir` (default: `tickets/`):

1. If preamble contains `Status: closed` (any case):
   - Remove the `Status:` line.
   - Append `Closed: migrated from Status: closed` to the preamble.
2. If preamble contains `Status: doing` or `Status: pending` or
   `Status: open` (any case):
   - Remove the `Status:` line. (Ticket becomes not-closed — correct.)
3. If no `Status:` line: no-op.

After processing all files, print a summary:
```
migrated: N tickets (K closed, M open/doing/pending stripped)
already clean: P tickets
```

Exit 0 always (migration is idempotent; running twice is safe).

Does NOT commit. User reviews the diff and commits manually (or the
migration instructions say to commit immediately).

### E. Tests

- Validator rejects `Status:` header (any value).
- Validator accepts `Closed:` in preamble; rejects it in log/body.
- `erg ready` excludes tickets with `Closed:` header.
- `erg ready` excludes tickets whose path contains `closed`.
- `erg close` appends `Closed: <reason>` to preamble; no Status line.
- `erg migrate`: closed ticket → `Closed:` added, `Status:` removed.
- `erg migrate`: open/doing/pending ticket → `Status:` removed, not closed.
- `erg migrate` idempotent: running twice produces same result.
- All existing tests pass.

## Migration instructions (for README / release notes)

1. Build and install the new binary.
2. Run `erg migrate tickets/` in each repo.
3. Review the diff (`git diff tickets/`).
4. Commit: `git commit -m "chore: migrate to Closed: header (erg migrate)"`.
5. Verify: `erg validate tickets/` → PASS.

The pre-commit hook will reject files with `Status:` lines after the
new binary is installed, so step 2 must precede any new commits.

## Out of scope

- Path convention for organizing closed tickets into subdirectories
  (left to each project; the path test makes any convention work).
- `erg archive` interaction (archive implies closed; no change needed —
  archive dir name contains `archive`, not `closed`, so path test
  doesn't fire; `Closed:` header in archived tickets is sufficient).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `rules/tickets.md` updated per §A
- [ ] Validator rejects `Status:`, accepts `Closed:` per §B
- [ ] `erg close` appends `Closed:` header per §C
- [ ] `erg migrate` converts all tickets atomically per §D
- [ ] Tests cover all cases in §E
- [ ] `make test` and `make validate` green on this repo's own tickets
      (after running `erg migrate` on them)
- [ ] Migration instructions documented
